+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P2] Tenant isolation never exercised: 0 tenants, all guests on tenant_default (bridge-20261027-tenant-dogfood)
+
+## Problem
+Verified live 2026-10-25:
+
+- `tenant_list` → `{"count": 0, "tenants": []}` — the full multi-tenant machinery (`tenant_create/update/suspend/activate/rotate_admin_token`, slot system, per-tenant admin tokens) has **never been exercised in production conditions**
+- `agent_status` shows every interactive client (`guest_generic_*`, `supreme-os-ucc`, `z-ai-assistant`) on `tenantId: "tenant_default"` — zero isolation in practice
+- AIQ-075 (P0 in the checklist) demands cross-tenant access + privilege-escalation tests before scale; the first real customer onboarding would be the first-ever test, at the worst possible moment
+
+## Impact (AIQ mapping)
+- AIQ-075 ❌ isolation unverified (P0 checklist item)
+- AIQ-047 🟡 permission boundaries designed but unproven under real tenancy
+- Blocks any B2B/agency pricing tier (AIQ-118/094)
+
+## Fix (smallest safe change)
+1. Dogfood: provision 2 internal tenants via `tenant_create` (e.g. `staging-admin`, `staging-customer`) with separate admin tokens
+2. Run the studio workspace against the customer tenant for one week; route at least one full agent work order through it
+3. Negative tests: customer-tenant token calls admin endpoints → expect 403 everywhere (scripted battery, results in CI); cross-tenant memory/doc reads → expect empty
+4. Document tenant limits (from `tenant_update` plan/limits fields) in the status page
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] `tenant_list` shows ≥1 active non-default tenant with its own admin token
+- [ ] Negative battery: 0 cross-tenant successes, all 403/empty as designed
+- [ ] One full work-order lifecycle completed inside the dogfood tenant
+- [ ] Findings filed as follow-ups if any isolation hole appears
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** untested isolation is equivalent to absent isolation; dogfooding converts a P0 unknown into a tested invariant at zero customer risk.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) waiting for a real customer — violates the checklist's own P0 rule; (b) synthetic load tests only — they miss the auth/UX seams that real usage finds.
+
+## Labels
+`bridge:queued` `P2-medium` `area:tenancy` `security` `AIQ:075` `AIQ:047`
